1
00:00:06,202 --> 00:00:08,228
One morning I noticed something simple.

2
00:00:08,308 --> 00:00:12,332
When I focus too hard on mental
work, I feel a lack of qi.

3
00:00:12,412 --> 00:00:15,298
It is as if thinking
itself uses the qi up.

4
00:00:16,118 --> 00:00:20,196
Then I exercise for half an
hour, and the qi is strong again.

5
00:00:20,276 --> 00:00:23,244
I felt it had something to
do with blood circulation.

6
00:00:24,066 --> 00:00:26,867
I am John Tan, known as Thusness.

7
00:00:26,947 --> 00:00:31,097
These are my own notes, from my
own practice and my own checking.

8
00:00:31,918 --> 00:00:33,686
So I asked a second question.

9
00:00:33,766 --> 00:00:37,749
Would it be better to move three
times a day, for a short time each?

10
00:00:37,829 --> 00:00:40,126
Once in the morning. Once at lunch.

11
00:00:40,206 --> 00:00:45,412
Once in the evening, after dinner. The
idea was simple. Keep the blood flowing.

12
00:00:45,492 --> 00:00:46,852
Keep the energy up.

13
00:00:46,932 --> 00:00:50,606
Clear the blockage that builds
when I concentrate for too long.

14
00:00:51,434 --> 00:00:53,420
I put both questions to an AI.

15
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:58,039
Later I asked another AI tool to check the
first answer against the research and the

16
00:00:58,119 --> 00:01:01,440
classical texts. Then
I checked both myself.

17
00:01:02,249 --> 00:01:04,628
What is left after that checking is short.

18
00:01:04,708 --> 00:01:06,408
The observation holds.

19
00:01:06,488 --> 00:01:08,446
The three-session plan holds too.

20
00:01:08,526 --> 00:01:12,006
But the most popular explanation
of why it works is wrong.

21
00:01:12,086 --> 00:01:15,651
And the correction is more
interesting than the original story.

22
00:01:16,488 --> 00:01:18,093
Here is the popular story.

23
00:01:18,173 --> 00:01:20,090
The first answer told it neatly.

24
00:01:20,170 --> 00:01:23,541
The brain is only about two
percent of the body's weight,

25
00:01:23,621 --> 00:01:27,060
yet it uses about twenty
percent of the body's energy.

26
00:01:27,140 --> 00:01:32,169
So when I think hard, it said, the
body sends a massive amount of sugar,

27
00:01:32,249 --> 00:01:34,859
oxygen and blood straight to the head.

28
00:01:34,939 --> 00:01:36,992
That drains the rest of the system.

29
00:01:37,072 --> 00:01:39,415
Blood and qi pool in the upper body.

30
00:01:40,225 --> 00:01:44,560
It sounds right. It matches the
feeling of a heavy, full head.

31
00:01:44,640 --> 00:01:46,453
But most of it does not hold up.

32
00:01:47,274 --> 00:01:51,977
Start with the numbers. The brain does
use about a fifth of the body's energy.

33
00:01:52,057 --> 00:01:56,298
But it uses that much all the
time. At rest. Even in sleep.

34
00:01:56,378 --> 00:01:59,382
Hard thinking adds only
a few percent on top.

35
00:01:59,462 --> 00:02:04,345
Solving a difficult problem costs the
brain little more than daydreaming does.

36
00:02:05,169 --> 00:02:09,246
And the body holds blood flow
to the brain steady. Tightly.

37
00:02:09,326 --> 00:02:13,540
The brain is not allowed to take a big
share of blood from the limbs just because

38
00:02:13,620 --> 00:02:17,879
I am concentrating. So thinking
does not drain the body's blood.

39
00:02:18,685 --> 00:02:20,575
Now the second part of the story.

40
00:02:20,655 --> 00:02:22,789
That blood and qi pool in the head.

41
00:02:22,869 --> 00:02:24,995
Here the truth runs the other way.

42
00:02:25,793 --> 00:02:31,297
In 2018, Sophie Carter and her colleagues
measured blood flow in a main artery of

43
00:02:31,377 --> 00:02:34,884
the brain. People sat for
four hours without a break.

44
00:02:34,964 --> 00:02:38,525
Over those hours, blood
flow to the brain went down.

45
00:02:38,605 --> 00:02:40,305
A little, but clearly.

46
00:02:40,385 --> 00:02:44,830
When the legs do not move, blood
returns to the heart more slowly.

47
00:02:44,910 --> 00:02:46,791
It settles in the lower body.

48
00:02:47,613 --> 00:02:51,976
In the same study, a two-minute easy
walk every half hour stopped the drop

49
00:02:52,056 --> 00:02:53,256
completely.

50
00:02:53,905 --> 00:02:58,838
So the heavy head and sluggish legs I feel
after a long morning at the desk do not

51
00:02:58,918 --> 00:03:01,148
come from too much blood up top.

52
00:03:01,228 --> 00:03:03,580
They come from too little movement below.

53
00:03:03,660 --> 00:03:06,886
And from something happening
inside the brain itself.

54
00:03:07,722 --> 00:03:09,123
That is the third part.

55
00:03:09,203 --> 00:03:14,028
The common idea is that a tired brain
has burned up its sugar. Run out of fuel.

56
00:03:14,108 --> 00:03:16,166
The research points somewhere else.

57
00:03:16,977 --> 00:03:21,693
In 2022, Antonius Wiehler and his
colleagues in Paris scanned people's

58
00:03:21,773 --> 00:03:25,443
brains at the start and the
end of a long working day.

59
00:03:25,523 --> 00:03:29,736
Those who did hard mental tasks all day
had more glutamate in the front of the

60
00:03:29,816 --> 00:03:34,995
brain by evening. Glutamate is a
chemical the brain uses to pass signals.

61
00:03:35,075 --> 00:03:40,013
These people also made more short-term,
impulsive choices as the day ended.

62
00:03:40,826 --> 00:03:46,140
The researchers suggest the brain slows
its own effortful control when glutamate

63
00:03:46,220 --> 00:03:49,048
builds up. A kind of protective brake.

64
00:03:49,128 --> 00:03:53,794
That is their hypothesis, not a
proven fact. And the study was small.

65
00:03:54,606 --> 00:03:57,719
But it fits my experience
better than running out of fuel.

66
00:03:57,799 --> 00:04:01,175
It feels less like an empty
tank. More like a jam.

67
00:04:02,002 --> 00:04:04,422
The first answer added one more image.

68
00:04:04,502 --> 00:04:08,852
Exercise, it said, flushes these
byproducts out of the brain.

69
00:04:08,932 --> 00:04:10,333
It is a nice image.

70
00:04:10,413 --> 00:04:14,314
But I found no study showing a short
workout washing glutamate out of the

71
00:04:14,394 --> 00:04:15,594
brain.

72
00:04:15,985 --> 00:04:17,549
What is shown is narrower.

73
00:04:17,629 --> 00:04:21,761
Short walking breaks keep blood
flow to the brain from falling.

74
00:04:21,841 --> 00:04:24,628
And exercise helps attention and mood.

75
00:04:24,708 --> 00:04:27,798
I keep the benefit, and
drop the flushing story.

76
00:04:28,613 --> 00:04:33,383
One more correction. Short, frequent
breaks are clearly better at one thing.

77
00:04:33,463 --> 00:04:36,237
They break up long sitting.
That is my problem.

78
00:04:36,316 --> 00:04:39,502
But it does not make one long
workout worse in general.

79
00:04:39,591 --> 00:04:41,440
For fitness, both count.

80
00:04:41,520 --> 00:04:46,196
The three-session plan is the right tool
for someone who thinks at a desk all day.

81
00:04:46,276 --> 00:04:48,184
It is not a law for everyone.

82
00:04:48,993 --> 00:04:52,776
Now the classical side. Here I
found the best anchor of all.

83
00:04:53,594 --> 00:04:58,487
The Yellow Emperor's Inner Classic is
the oldest classic of Chinese medicine.

84
00:04:58,567 --> 00:05:03,229
In the part called Suwen, chapter
thirty-nine lists nine ways that states of

85
00:05:03,309 --> 00:05:05,077
mind change the qi.

86
00:05:05,157 --> 00:05:09,375
On thinking, it says four
words: thinking knots the qi.

87
00:05:10,193 --> 00:05:14,814
Then it explains. When one thinks,
the heart holds on to something,

88
00:05:14,894 --> 00:05:16,797
and the spirit gathers there.

89
00:05:16,877 --> 00:05:19,773
The upright qi stays, and does not move.

90
00:05:19,853 --> 00:05:21,462
So the qi is knotted.

91
00:05:22,269 --> 00:05:23,670
This is precise.

92
00:05:23,750 --> 00:05:28,113
And it agrees with the modern findings
better than the popular story does.

93
00:05:28,193 --> 00:05:31,170
The text does not say
thinking burns up the qi.

94
00:05:31,250 --> 00:05:36,269
It says thinking makes the qi stay,
and not move. Stuck, not empty.

95
00:05:37,094 --> 00:05:40,683
That matches sitting still
while blood settles in the legs.

96
00:05:40,763 --> 00:05:44,165
It matches a brain that is
jammed rather than out of fuel.

97
00:05:44,981 --> 00:05:48,678
The AI report also had the
classics wrong in places.

98
00:05:48,758 --> 00:05:54,507
It placed the saying "thinking injures
the Spleen" in the Lingshu, chapter eight.

99
00:05:54,587 --> 00:05:57,577
The saying is from the
Suwen, chapter five.

100
00:05:57,657 --> 00:06:00,743
The Lingshu says something
close but different:

101
00:06:00,823 --> 00:06:03,556
when worry in the Spleen is not resolved,

102
00:06:03,636 --> 00:06:05,299
it injures the intention.

103
00:06:06,118 --> 00:06:10,984
The report also said the old classic
teaches that a weak Spleen fails to make

104
00:06:11,064 --> 00:06:14,639
Heart Blood, so the spirit
cannot settle at night.

105
00:06:14,719 --> 00:06:18,919
That idea belongs to later Chinese
medicine. It may be useful.

106
00:06:18,999 --> 00:06:20,880
But it should carry its own date.

107
00:06:21,685 --> 00:06:25,056
And it used a saying from
qigong and taijiquan:

108
00:06:25,136 --> 00:06:27,678
where the mind goes, the qi goes.

109
00:06:27,758 --> 00:06:30,069
In practice, that is a principle.

110
00:06:30,149 --> 00:06:32,162
You guide the qi with attention.

111
00:06:32,242 --> 00:06:37,479
Reading it as a cause of illness is the
report's own idea, not the tradition's.

112
00:06:38,310 --> 00:06:40,377
There is a sound point inside it, though.

113
00:06:40,457 --> 00:06:44,711
If attention sits in the head for
hours, everything gathers there.

114
00:06:44,791 --> 00:06:48,996
Nothing moves below. Chinese
medicine has a name for this pattern:

115
00:06:49,085 --> 00:06:51,681
excess above, deficiency below.

116
00:06:51,761 --> 00:06:54,779
As a description of how
it feels, it fits well.

117
00:06:54,859 --> 00:06:58,778
As a claim about blood piling
up in the skull, it does not.

118
00:06:59,602 --> 00:07:04,278
The Taoist tradition speaks of
three treasures. Jing, essence.

119
00:07:04,358 --> 00:07:06,370
Qi, breath and energy.

120
00:07:06,450 --> 00:07:08,598
And shen, spirit and mind.

121
00:07:08,678 --> 00:07:13,897
Inner alchemy treats them as one life
force at different degrees of fineness.

122
00:07:13,977 --> 00:07:17,389
Its classic path refines essence into qi,

123
00:07:17,469 --> 00:07:19,201
and qi into spirit.

124
00:07:20,017 --> 00:07:22,912
A teaching image I find
useful is a candle.

125
00:07:22,992 --> 00:07:28,510
Jing is the wax and the wick: the
body's deep reserves and basic health.

126
00:07:28,590 --> 00:07:33,483
Qi is the flame: breath,
circulation, the living movement.

127
00:07:33,563 --> 00:07:37,618
Shen is the light:
awareness, focus, thinking.

128
00:07:38,429 --> 00:07:43,294
Read this way, a long morning of hard
thinking is a bright light with a flame

129
00:07:43,374 --> 00:07:47,289
that is not being fed, because
the body is not moving.

130
00:07:47,369 --> 00:07:51,582
The spirit gathers in one
place, and the qi stops moving.

131
00:07:51,662 --> 00:07:55,133
Exercise feeds the flame,
and moves it again.

132
00:07:55,966 --> 00:07:58,916
I keep this as a
description, not a mechanism.

133
00:07:58,996 --> 00:08:02,870
Blood flow, glutamate and sitting
are what happens in the body.

134
00:08:02,950 --> 00:08:08,685
Jing, qi and shen are a way of feeling and
naming the whole of it from the inside.

135
00:08:08,765 --> 00:08:10,429
The two do not compete.

136
00:08:11,245 --> 00:08:13,189
And qi is not a hidden stuff.

137
00:08:13,269 --> 00:08:16,763
In its first meaning, qi
was vapour and breath.

138
00:08:16,843 --> 00:08:19,616
It is not a substance
standing behind warmth,

139
00:08:19,696 --> 00:08:21,735
movement and alertness.

140
00:08:21,815 --> 00:08:26,273
When I say my qi is weak, I mean
the body feels heavy and slow,

141
00:08:26,353 --> 00:08:27,972
and the mind feels dull.

142
00:08:28,052 --> 00:08:31,436
When I say my qi is
strong, I mean the reverse.

143
00:08:31,516 --> 00:08:33,977
The words point to how
the body is working.

144
00:08:34,057 --> 00:08:36,808
Not to a fluid that thinking drains away.

145
00:08:37,625 --> 00:08:41,353
So here is the plan I asked about,
with what the checking adds.

146
00:08:42,165 --> 00:08:46,596
In the morning, movement wakes the body
and gets the blood going before the day's

147
00:08:46,676 --> 00:08:51,206
desk work. Feed the flame before
the light is asked to shine.

148
00:08:52,009 --> 00:08:55,638
At lunch, a walk breaks up
a long morning of sitting,

149
00:08:55,718 --> 00:08:58,505
and brings blood flow
to the brain back up.

150
00:08:58,585 --> 00:09:01,172
It unties the knot that thinking tied.

151
00:09:01,973 --> 00:09:06,852
In the evening, an easy walk after dinner
lowers the rise in blood sugar after a

152
00:09:06,932 --> 00:09:10,588
meal, because working muscles
take up sugar on their own.

153
00:09:10,668 --> 00:09:14,420
Kept gentle, it helps the
body wind down for sleep.

154
00:09:14,500 --> 00:09:17,137
The qi comes down from
the head to the belly,

155
00:09:17,217 --> 00:09:21,394
so the spirit can rest and the
essence can recover overnight.

156
00:09:22,222 --> 00:09:24,384
The checking added one more piece.

157
00:09:24,464 --> 00:09:28,827
Brain blood flow drops when sitting
goes on for hours without a break.

158
00:09:28,907 --> 00:09:32,876
So three sessions may not be enough
on their own during a long morning of

159
00:09:32,956 --> 00:09:36,708
writing. Getting up for a short
walk in between matters too.

160
00:09:36,788 --> 00:09:40,041
The study tested two
minutes, every half hour.

161
00:09:40,861 --> 00:09:42,302
And one thing I dropped.

162
00:09:42,382 --> 00:09:47,194
The report said morning exercise boosts
the rise in cortisol that comes after

163
00:09:47,274 --> 00:09:51,859
waking. I could not find good support
for that. So it is not in my plan.

164
00:09:52,659 --> 00:09:55,147
A last word on checking AI answers.

165
00:09:55,227 --> 00:09:57,783
The first answer was warm and fluent.

166
00:09:57,863 --> 00:10:02,470
It called my observation profoundly
accurate, and my plan perfect.

167
00:10:02,550 --> 00:10:07,267
But its central explanation, blood
rushing to the head, was wrong.

168
00:10:07,347 --> 00:10:08,834
Praise is not proof.

169
00:10:09,658 --> 00:10:12,690
The second, a research report, was better.

170
00:10:12,770 --> 00:10:16,793
It corrected the blood-flow
story and cited two good studies.

171
00:10:16,873 --> 00:10:19,959
But it also misplaced
classical quotations.

172
00:10:20,039 --> 00:10:22,771
It stretched one study
further than it went.

173
00:10:22,851 --> 00:10:25,896
And it listed several sources
I could not trace at all.

174
00:10:25,976 --> 00:10:28,301
One was called a peer-reviewed preprint.

175
00:10:28,381 --> 00:10:31,227
A preprint is a paper before peer review.

176
00:10:32,041 --> 00:10:36,635
What survived the checking is
small, but solid. My own experience.

177
00:10:36,715 --> 00:10:39,751
One line from the Suwen. And two studies.

178
00:10:40,578 --> 00:10:41,778
That is enough.

